/surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Two collagen-binding proteins, osteonectin and HSP47, are coordinately induced in transformed keratinocytes by heat and other stresses.</article-title><source>Exp Cell Res</source><volume>212</volume><fpage>219</fpage><lpage>224</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8187816</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001029-Emerson1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Emerson</surname><given-names>RO</given-names></name><name><surname>Sage</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghosh</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>JI</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Chaperone-like activity revealed in the matricellular protein SPARC.</article-title><source>J Cell Biochem</source><volume>98</volume><fpage>701</fpage><lpage>705</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16598771</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001029-Vranka1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vranka</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakai</surname><given-names>LY</given-names></name><name><surname>Bachinger</surname><given-names>HP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Prolyl 3-hydroxylase 1, enzyme characterization and identification of a novel family of enzymes.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>279</volume><fpage>23615</fpage><lpage>23621</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15044469</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001029-Barnes1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Morello</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Cabral</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Weis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Deficiency of cartilage-associated protein in recessive lethal osteogenesis imperfecta.</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><volume>355</volume><fpage>2757</fpage><lpage>2764</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17192541</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001029-Cabral1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cabral</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Weis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Prolyl 3-hydroxylase 1 deficiency causes a recessive metabolic bone disorder resembling lethal/severe osteogenesis imperfecta.</article-title><source>Nat Genet</source><volume>39</volume><fpage>359</fpage><lpage>365</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17277775</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001029-Morello1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morello</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bertin</surname><given-names>TK</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hicks</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tonachini</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>CRTAP is required for prolyl 3- hydroxylation and mutations cause recessive osteogenesis imperfecta.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>127</volume><fpage>291</fpage><lpage>304</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17055431</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001029-Fink1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fink</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Chaperone-mediated protein folding.</article-title><source>Physiol Rev</source><volume>79</volume><fpage>425</fpage><lpage>449</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10221986</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001029-Young1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Agashe</surname><given-names>VR</given-names></name><name><surname>Siegers</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hartl</surname><given-names>FU</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Pathways of chaperone-mediated protein folding in the cytosol.</article-title><source>Nat Rev Mol Cell Biol</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>781</fpage><lpage>791</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15459659</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001029-Macdonald1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Macdonald</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bachinger</surname><given-names>HP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>HSP47 binds cooperatively to triple helical type I collagen but has little effect on the thermal stability or rate of refolding.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>276</volume><fpage>25399</fpage><lpage>25403</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11333272</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001029-Sauk1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sauk</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Nikitakis</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Siavash</surname><given-names>H<